name valley_far
describe A 300 m view down a valley. The distance/LOD look shot: everything past the finest ring is a coarser node, so this is where the LOD ladder's seams, the moire Prompt 005 is about, and the fog Prompt 007 derives all become visible at once.
backend both

# TAA off for every scenario that compares a capture against a golden. Measured, not assumed:
# with TAA on, vk-vs-vk moves 0.996% of pixels at this pose against a 1.5% gate, and with it off
# 0.341% -- see dev/harness/src/image_compare.hpp for the full four-case table.
option --no-taa

pose_ground 48,0 -90 -8 12
wait 2

capture end valley_far

assert frames > 0
assert contrast_percent > 6

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ goal 273: the regression gate
# A PERCENTILE of the GPU timestamp range across this fixed camera path, per research section 6.8 --
# never a mean (one hitch moves it) and above all never fps, which this machine's 165 Hz
# FIFO_RELAXED panel caps at 155-159 and which therefore cannot express a regression at all.
#
# PER BACKEND, because vk and d3d12 differ by 30-35% here and `ctest -L scenario` runs vk ONLY. A
# single threshold would have to be set by the slower backend, leaving the faster one 35% of slack
# -- a 30% vk regression would sail straight through the gate that CI actually runs.
#
# Each number is ~1.2x the worst of three runs on THAT backend: the smallest margin that survives
# run-to-run noise and still fails when the budget is tightened by 20%, which is goal 273's own
# Check and is demonstrated in the log.
#
# AND THE MEDIAN HERE, not the p95. This scenario runs ~320 frames, where the 95th percentile is the
# sixteenth-worst frame and therefore one hitch away from anything. Measured on BOTH backends:
#
#   vk    p95 4.76 3.68 3.53 (35% spread)  |  median 2.93 3.02 3.00 (3%)
#   d3d12 p95 4.45 4.93 5.92 6.46 (45%)    |  median 3.78 3.95 3.98 4.03 (7%)
#
# The long scenarios above gate on p95, where it holds to 2%. A p95 needs roughly 800 frames on this
# machine before it is a statistic rather than a coin flip -- the table lives in
# dev/scenario/include/dev/scenario/assertion.hpp.
assert gpu_ms_median < 3.6 vk
assert gpu_ms_median < 4.6 d3d12
